# LF in the working tree on every platform, Windows included.
#
# Not cosmetic: the parser reports byte offsets, the identity and parity sweeps
# compare spans, and the WIT/DOT snapshots are byte-compared. A CRLF checkout
# shifts every offset past the first newline and fails those tests for a reason
# that has nothing to do with the change under test. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, so the CI matrix needs this to be stated, not assumed.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.vsix binary
